Hello Citizens! 

Here we are with the latest HotFix Update for Hell is Others! 
Before looking at the other fixes, just a few words about one of the most important parts of the Update: the new duos design. You have pointed out several times the problem of the unreadable "companions" during your games. We decided to solve this by changing some of the rules related to duos: 


 The Other partner has a blu area at its feet to differentiate it from enemies.
 We also make it possible to extract two players from the same lift if they are part of the same team.

We’ll check your feedback to know if this new design matches your expectations! 

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/39298344/8324531a9d12657e400399484b9b2681dcf4786e.gif

We’ve also worked on a bunch of bugs and problems that you have pointed out to us! Here’s the full list:


 Fixed a bug where players got blocked (so they cannot continue the story) closing the game right after talking with Isolde during Act II;
 Fixed a bug where players can skip Alfred's mandatory dialogues if they go to sleep with a perishable item in the inventory, causing the player to be stuck during the story;
 Fixed the bug that caused the player to not have the updated map (the player stayed with the tutorial map);
 Fixed an issue on reconnection in case of a player in a party;
 Fixed a bug that caused some rewards to disappear from quests with modified bullets as rewards;
 We made prestige paintings priceless in order to make the story progression fairer.

Thanks again for your attention, Citizens!

Hello Citizens!

With these new patch notes, we fixed some of the bugs and technical problems that we found after the Winter Helliday update. We're also adding some details to certain elements of the game that we think you'll appreciate! Here's the full list:


 Fixed imagos not getting set upon spawning in the shops;
 Fixed pocket being exploitable during the tutorial;
 Fixed the last item of the referral system's gift box reappearing at every new login;
 Fixed gift box sorting layer;
 Added splash sound effect when throwing an object inside the water;
 Added sound effects when receiving Octave's quest rewards;
 Imagos are now updated when loading the game to make sure they are always correct and with the number of points indicated on their configuration;
 Reduced Imagos provided by the Wall Safe;
 Green weapons are now a lot more common, spawning up to 4 times more across Century City;
 Drinks no longer increase or decrease satiety. That also means that Attributes are now capped equally for everyone;
 We reduced Mr Chapman's and Mr Watt's range to have a more varied weapons meta;


Now your hunt should be a little smoother! Let us know here, in the official discord channel.
